IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Montana Code Annotated 2025, Title 15, chapter 30 (individual income tax), parts 21 and 23 -- the seat-neutral core:
-- who is a resident (15-30-2101(31)), Montana taxable income from federal taxable income (15-30-2101(22), 15-30-2120),
-- the rates for tax year 2026 (15-30-2103, temporary version) and from 2027 (15-30-2103, version effective 1 January
-- 2027), the nonresident ratio (15-30-2104(1)), the duty to file on a change of residence (15-30-2112), the earned
-- income tax credit (15-30-2318) and the residential property tax credit for the elderly (15-30-2337 to 15-30-2341).
--
-- Edition: Montana Code Annotated 2025 (laws through the 2025 session), site marked "Updated August 2026", as deposited
-- at ../../registers/source-bundle/mca-15-30-part-21.txt and mca-15-30-part-23.txt (retrieved 2026-10-19 UTC).
--
-- Federal taxable income (IRC s 63), federal adjusted gross income (IRC s 62), filing status (IRC ss 2, 7703) and the
-- federal earned income credit (IRC s 32) are borrowed terms, taken as inputs. They are encoded federally in
-- subjects/us/internal-revenue-code-of-1986/ (cross-folder IMPORT is not possible in the stable l4; NOTES.md names the
-- link).
--
-- The seat questions are in mt-iit-seat.l4. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Montana individual income tax -- core`

§§ `Questions this encoding does not cover`

DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    `tax years before 2026: only the 2026 (temporary) and 2027 versions of 15-30-2103 are deposited`
    `tax years after 2027: the brackets are the department's inflation-adjusted brackets under 15-30-2103(3), and none was given`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH A TYPE
DECLARE `Answer` a IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `the answer` IS AN a
    `not covered` HAS `because`    IS A `Why not covered`

§§ `15-30-2101(31) -- resident`

-- "Resident" applies only to natural persons and includes "any person domiciled in the state of Montana and any other
-- person who maintains a permanent place of abode within the state even though temporarily absent from the state and
-- who has not established a residence elsewhere".
GIVEN `domiciled in Montana` IS A BOOLEAN
      `maintains a permanent place of abode in Montana` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has established a residence elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a Montana resident` IF
        `domiciled in Montana`
    OR  (    `maintains a permanent place of abode in Montana`
         AND (NOT `has established a residence elsewhere`))

§§ `15-30-2120 -- Montana taxable income`

-- 15-30-2101(22): "Montana taxable income" means federal taxable income as determined for federal income tax purposes
-- and adjusted as provided in 15-30-2120. 15-30-2120(1): the items in (2) are added and the items in (3) are subtracted.
-- 15-30-2113: filing status, dependent status and every other status is the one claimed on the federal return.
DECLARE `Filing status` IS ONE OF
    `married filing jointly or surviving spouse`
    `head of household`
    `single`
    `married filing separately`

DECLARE `Federal return figures` HAS
    `federal taxable income`                         IS A NUMBER
    `state income taxes deducted as an itemized deduction` IS A NUMBER
    `federal itemized deductions in total`           IS A NUMBER
    `federal standard deduction allowable`           IS A NUMBER
    `qualified business income deduction claimed`    IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Montana adjustments` HAS
    -- 15-30-2120(2)(a)
    `interest on other states' and territories' obligations not exempt under federal law` IS A NUMBER
    -- 15-30-2120(2)(b) to (h) and (k), as one figure
    `other additions under 15-30-2120(2)`            IS A NUMBER
    -- 15-30-2120(3)(b)
    `US obligation interest and railroad retirement benefits exempt under federal law` IS A NUMBER
    -- 15-30-2120(3)(c)
    `armed forces and national guard active-duty salary subtraction` IS A NUMBER
    -- 15-30-2120(3)(g), (7)
    `number of taxpayers on the return aged 65 or over` IS A NUMBER
    `the age 65 subtraction for the year as indexed by the department` IS A NUMBER
    -- 15-30-2120(6)
    `ABLE account contributions`                     IS A NUMBER
    -- 15-30-2120(3)(a), (d)-(f), (h)-(q), (4), (5), (8)-(11), as one figure
    `other subtractions under 15-30-2120(3) to (5)`  IS A NUMBER

-- 15-30-2120(2)(j): for an individual who deducts state income taxes under IRC s 164(a)(3), "an additional amount equal
-- to the state income tax deduction claimed, not to exceed the amount required to reduce the federal itemized amount
-- ... to the amount of the federal standard deduction allowable under section 63(c)". Read as: the lesser of the state
-- income tax deducted and the excess of the itemized total over the standard deduction (never below zero).
GIVEN f IS A `Federal return figures`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the state income tax add-back` f MEANS
    min (f's `state income taxes deducted as an itemized deduction`)
        (max 0 (f's `federal itemized deductions in total` MINUS f's `federal standard deduction allowable`))

-- 15-30-2120(6)(a): "may reduce taxable income by the lesser of $3,000 or the amount of the contribution"; joint
-- filers "not in excess of $6,000". Not indexed.
GIVEN status IS A `Filing status`, contributions IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the ABLE subtraction` status contributions MEANS
    IF status EQUALS `married filing jointly or surviving spouse`
    THEN min contributions 6000
    ELSE min contributions 3000

GIVEN status IS A `Filing status`, f IS A `Federal return figures`, adj IS A `Montana adjustments`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Montana taxable income` status f adj MEANS
    (f's `federal taxable income` PLUS additions) MINUS subtractions
    WHERE
        additions MEANS
                adj's `interest on other states' and territories' obligations not exempt under federal law`
            PLUS adj's `other additions under 15-30-2120(2)`
            PLUS f's `qualified business income deduction claimed`
            PLUS `the state income tax add-back` f
        subtractions MEANS
                adj's `US obligation interest and railroad retirement benefits exempt under federal law`
            PLUS adj's `armed forces and national guard active-duty salary subtraction`
            PLUS (adj's `number of taxpayers on the return aged 65 or over` TIMES adj's `the age 65 subtraction for the year as indexed by the department`)
            PLUS `the ABLE subtraction` status (adj's `ABLE account contributions`)
            PLUS adj's `other subtractions under 15-30-2120(3) to (5)`

§§ `15-30-2103 -- rate of tax`

-- The ceiling of the 4.7% bracket, and the top rate.
-- Tax year 2026, 15-30-2103 (Temporary), terminating 31 December 2026: joint and surviving spouse $95,000; head of
-- household $71,250; single and married filing separately $47,500; top rate 5.65%. No indexing in this version.
-- From 1 January 2027: $130,000; $97,500; $65,000; $65,000; top rate 5.4%; (3) the department multiplies the brackets
-- by the "modified inflation factor" (CPI-U for June of the previous tax year divided by CPI-U for June 2026, (4)(a)
-- with 15-30-2101(12)) and rounds to the nearest $100. For tax year 2027 the factor is CPI June 2026 / CPI June 2026 = 1,
-- so the statutory figures apply unchanged (NOTES.md finding 2). From 2028 the published bracket is an input.
DECLARE `Rate schedule` HAS
    `the 4.7% bracket ceiling` IS A NUMBER
    `the top rate`             IS A NUMBER

GIVEN status IS A `Filing status`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 2026 bracket ceiling` status MEANS
    CONSIDER status
    WHEN `married filing jointly or surviving spouse` THEN 95000
    WHEN `head of household`                          THEN 71250
    WHEN `single`                                     THEN 47500
    WHEN `married filing separately`                  THEN 47500

GIVEN status IS A `Filing status`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 2027 statutory bracket ceiling` status MEANS
    CONSIDER status
    WHEN `married filing jointly or surviving spouse` THEN 130000
    WHEN `head of household`                          THEN 97500
    WHEN `single`                                     THEN 65000
    WHEN `married filing separately`                  THEN 65000

-- `the department's published bracket ceiling` is used only for tax years after 2027; 0 means not given.
GIVEN `tax year` IS A NUMBER
      status IS A `Filing status`
      `the department's published bracket ceiling` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Answer` `Rate schedule`
`the rate schedule for` `tax year` status `the department's published bracket ceiling` MEANS
    IF `tax year` LESS THAN 2026
    THEN `not covered` `tax years before 2026: only the 2026 (temporary) and 2027 versions of 15-30-2103 are deposited`
    ELSE IF `tax year` EQUALS 2026
         THEN `answered` (`Rate schedule` WITH `the 4.7% bracket ceiling` IS `the 2026 bracket ceiling` status, `the top rate` IS 0.0565)
         ELSE IF `tax year` EQUALS 2027
              THEN `answered` (`Rate schedule` WITH `the 4.7% bracket ceiling` IS `the 2027 statutory bracket ceiling` status, `the top rate` IS 0.054)
              ELSE IF `the department's published bracket ceiling` GREATER THAN 0
                   THEN `answered` (`Rate schedule` WITH `the 4.7% bracket ceiling` IS `the department's published bracket ceiling`, `the top rate` IS 0.054)
                   ELSE `not covered` `tax years after 2027: the brackets are the department's inflation-adjusted brackets under 15-30-2103(3), and none was given`

-- 15-30-2103(1): 4.7% "on the first [ceiling] of Montana taxable income or any part of that income", the top rate "on
-- any Montana taxable income in excess of [ceiling]".
GIVEN income IS A NUMBER, schedule IS A `Rate schedule`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the ordinary tax on` income schedule MEANS
        (0.047 TIMES (min (max 0 income) (schedule's `the 4.7% bracket ceiling`)))
    PLUS (schedule's `the top rate` TIMES (max 0 (income MINUS schedule's `the 4.7% bracket ceiling`)))

-- 15-30-2103(2): the portion of Montana taxable income that consists of net long-term capital gains (IRC s 1222) is
-- taxed at 3.0% "on the first [ceiling] less nonqualified taxable income" and 4.1% above; "if the total nonqualified
-- taxable income is [ceiling] or greater, all of the net long-term capital gains are taxed at 4.1%". (3)(b)/(4)(c):
-- nonqualified taxable income is Montana taxable income that is not net long-term capital gains. The capital gains
-- portion is read as never more than Montana taxable income itself. 15-30-3704 (an exception) is not deposited.
GIVEN mti IS A NUMBER, ltcg IS A NUMBER, schedule IS A `Rate schedule`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the resident tax on` mti ltcg schedule MEANS
    `the ordinary tax on` nonqualified schedule
        PLUS (0.03 TIMES at3)
        PLUS (0.041 TIMES (gains MINUS at3))
    WHERE
        gains MEANS max 0 (min ltcg mti)
        nonqualified MEANS max 0 (mti MINUS gains)
        at3 MEANS min gains (max 0 (schedule's `the 4.7% bracket ceiling` MINUS nonqualified))

-- 15-30-2104(1)(a): a nonresident's tax is the tax computed under 15-30-2103 "as if the nonresident ... were a resident
-- during the entire tax year, multiplied by the ratio of Montana source income to total income from all sources".
-- (Montana source income, 15-30-2101(21), includes everything received while a resident, so the same ratio is used for
-- a part-year resident; NOTES.md finding 4.) 15-30-2106 (the nonresident compensation exclusion) is an input: leave
-- the excluded compensation out of Montana source income.
GIVEN `full-year tax` IS A NUMBER, `Montana source income` IS A NUMBER, `total income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the nonresident tax` `full-year tax` `Montana source income` `total income` MEANS
    IF `total income` AT MOST 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE `full-year tax` TIMES (`Montana source income` DIVIDED BY `total income`)

§§ `15-30-2318 -- earned income tax credit`

-- (1), (2): a resident taxpayer is allowed a credit of 20% of the federal earned income credit under IRC s 32.
-- (3), (5)(b): reduced by the "reduction percentage", the earned income treated as a dividend from a s 501(d)
-- agricultural organization divided by total earned income. (4): refundable.
GIVEN resident IS A BOOLEAN
      `federal earned income credit` IS A NUMBER
      `earned income` IS A NUMBER
      `earned income treated as a 501(d) dividend` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Montana earned income tax credit` resident `federal earned income credit` `earned income` `earned income treated as a 501(d) dividend` MEANS
    IF (NOT resident)
    THEN 0
    ELSE (0.2 TIMES `federal earned income credit`) TIMES (1 MINUS reduction)
    WHERE
        reduction MEANS
            IF `earned income` GREATER THAN 0
            THEN min 1 (`earned income treated as a 501(d) dividend` DIVIDED BY `earned income`)
            ELSE 0

§§ `15-30-2337 to 15-30-2341 -- residential property tax credit for the elderly`

DECLARE `Elderly claim` HAS
    `reached 62 or older during the claim period`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `months resided in Montana in the period`          IS A NUMBER
    `months occupied a Montana dwelling as owner, renter or lessee` IS A NUMBER
    `gross household income`                           IS A NUMBER
    -- 15-30-2337(10), less any portion derived from a public rent or tax subsidy program (15-30-2341(2))
    `property tax billed on the owned homestead`       IS A NUMBER
    -- 15-30-2337(5), likewise
    `gross rent paid for the rented homestead`         IS A NUMBER
    -- 15-30-2341(3)
    `the rented dwelling is subject to Montana property tax or rented from a housing authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- 15-30-2341(1)
    `another member of the household claims for the period` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- 15-30-2338(3), the department's finding
    `the department finds title was received primarily to get the credit` IS A BOOLEAN

-- 15-30-2338(1): age 62 or older during the claim period; resided in Montana at least 9 months of it; occupied one or
-- more Montana dwellings as owner, renter or lessee at least 6 months; "less than $45,000 of gross household income".
-- 15-30-2341(1): one claimant per household; 15-30-2338(3): disallowed if title was taken primarily for the credit.
GIVEN c IS AN `Elderly claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is eligible for the elderly credit` c IF
        c's `reached 62 or older during the claim period`
    AND c's `months resided in Montana in the period` AT LEAST 9
    AND c's `months occupied a Montana dwelling as owner, renter or lessee` AT LEAST 6
    AND c's `gross household income` LESS THAN 45000
    AND (NOT c's `another member of the household claims for the period`)
    AND (NOT c's `the department finds title was received primarily to get the credit`)

-- 15-30-2337(8): "household income" is gross household income less $12,600.
GIVEN `gross household income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`household income` `gross household income` MEANS `gross household income` MINUS 12600

-- 15-30-2340(4): the reduction, "the product of [rate] times the household income", by $1,000 band.
GIVEN hi IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the reduction rate` hi MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF hi LESS THAN 2000 THEN 0
        IF hi LESS THAN 3000 THEN 0.006
        IF hi LESS THAN 4000 THEN 0.016
        IF hi LESS THAN 5000 THEN 0.024
        IF hi LESS THAN 6000 THEN 0.028
        IF hi LESS THAN 7000 THEN 0.032
        IF hi LESS THAN 8000 THEN 0.035
        IF hi LESS THAN 9000 THEN 0.039
        IF hi LESS THAN 10000 THEN 0.042
        IF hi LESS THAN 11000 THEN 0.045
        IF hi LESS THAN 12000 THEN 0.048
        OTHERWISE 0.05

GIVEN hi IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the reduction` hi MEANS `the reduction rate` hi TIMES (max 0 hi)

-- 15-30-2340(5): for gross household income from $35,000 to under $45,000, only a percentage of the credit. The
-- subsection's opening words say "household income", the table's column says "gross household income"; this encoding
-- follows the table (NOTES.md finding 5).
GIVEN ghi IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the percentage of credit allowed` ghi MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF ghi LESS THAN 35000 THEN 1
        IF ghi AT MOST 37500 THEN 0.4
        IF ghi AT MOST 40000 THEN 0.3
        IF ghi AT MOST 42500 THEN 0.2
        IF ghi LESS THAN 45000 THEN 0.1
        OTHERWISE 0

-- 15-30-2340(1)-(3): owner: property tax billed less the reduction; renter: rent-equivalent tax paid (15% of gross rent,
-- 15-30-2337(11)) less the reduction; both: each portion less the reduction (the text takes the reduction from each
-- portion; NOTES.md finding 6). A portion never goes below zero. (6): at most $1,150.
GIVEN c IS AN `Elderly claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the elderly credit` c MEANS
    IF `is eligible for the elderly credit` c
    THEN min 1150 ((owned PLUS rented) TIMES (`the percentage of credit allowed` (c's `gross household income`)))
    ELSE 0
    WHERE
        r MEANS `the reduction` (`household income` (c's `gross household income`))
        owned MEANS
            IF c's `property tax billed on the owned homestead` GREATER THAN 0
            THEN max 0 (c's `property tax billed on the owned homestead` MINUS r)
            ELSE 0
        rented MEANS
            IF     c's `gross rent paid for the rented homestead` GREATER THAN 0
               AND c's `the rented dwelling is subject to Montana property tax or rented from a housing authority`
            THEN max 0 ((0.15 TIMES c's `gross rent paid for the rented homestead`) MINUS r)
            ELSE 0

§§ `Duties and deadlines`

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the taxpayer`
    `the claimant`
    `the department of revenue`

DECLARE `Act` IS ONE OF
    `file a Montana income tax return`
    `submit the elderly credit claim with the property tax or rent receipt`
    `revise the return and make the elderly credit claim`
    
-- 15-30-2112: "If a taxpayer changes status from that of resident to that of nonresident or from that of nonresident to
-- that of resident during the tax year, the taxpayer shall file a return." The due date is in part 26 (not deposited),
-- so the days from the end of the tax year to it are an input.
GIVEN `days to the return due date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the duty to file on a change of residence` `days to the return due date` MEANS
    PARTY `the taxpayer`
    MUST  `file a Montana income tax return`
    WITHIN `days to the return due date`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the taxpayer` BECAUSE "a taxpayer who changed residence status during the year did not file the return 15-30-2112 requires"

-- 15-30-2339(1): the claim "must be submitted at the same time the claimant's individual income tax return is due";
-- for an individual not required to file, "on or before April 15 of the year following"; (2) with the receipt.
-- (3): "The department may grant a reasonable extension for filing a claim whenever, in its judgment, good cause exists."
-- (5): the individual "may revise a return and make a claim ... within 3 years from the last day prescribed".
GIVEN `days to the last day for the claim` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the elderly credit claim deadline` `days to the last day for the claim` MEANS
    PARTY `the claimant`
    MUST  `submit the elderly credit claim with the property tax or rent receipt`
    WITHIN `days to the last day for the claim`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "the elderly credit claim was not submitted by the last day; only a department extension for good cause (15-30-2339(3)) or a revision within 3 years (15-30-2339(5)) remains"

-- The last day for the claim (15-30-2339(1)): the return due date if the claimant must file, otherwise April 15 of the
-- following year, moved to the first business day after it where April 15 is an IRS-recognised holiday not observed in
-- Montana (an input, given as that business day).
GIVEN `required to file a Montana return` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the return due date` IS A DATE
      `claim period year` IS A NUMBER
      `the first business day after a deferring holiday on April 15, if any` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the elderly credit claim` `required to file a Montana return` `the return due date` `claim period year` `the first business day after a deferring holiday on April 15, if any` MEANS
    IF `required to file a Montana return`
    THEN `the return due date`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the first business day after a deferring holiday on April 15, if any`
         WHEN JUST d THEN d
         WHEN NOTHING THEN Date 15 4 (`claim period year` PLUS 1)

-- 15-30-2339(5): a revision and claim "within 3 years from the last day prescribed for filing a claim for relief".
GIVEN `the last day for the claim` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to revise and claim` `the last day for the claim` MEANS
    Date (DATE_DAY `the last day for the claim`) (DATE_MONTH `the last day for the claim`) (DATE_YEAR `the last day for the claim` PLUS 3)
